      },
      {
        "introduction": "So that all will know that the eventual release of the people of Israel is due not to mere chance or changing political winds, God directs Jeremiah to record God's promises regarding the restoration. Using the prophetic poetry he often employs, Jeremiah makes it clear that it will be the God of Israel who purposely restores his people—nothing else."
